SUMMARY:TIFF Next Wave Film Festival
DESCRIPTION:TIFF Next Wave Film Festival returns for its 15th edition with a weekend of youth-driven international cinema curated by the TIFF Next Wave Committee — a group of 12 teens from across the GTA. The festival features nine international feature films\, filmmaker Q&As\, workshops\, live events\, and special programs designed for young audiences. Opening night begins with the Canadian Premiere of Roommates (dir. Chandler Levack)\, followed by Our Hero\, Balthazar (dir. Oscar Boyson). Later\, join us for the Opening Night Party\, themed “Motion Blur\,” an immersive celebration to kick off the weekend. \nHighlights: \n\nCanadian Premiere of Roommates opens the festival\nOur Hero\, Balthazar follows on opening night\nOpening Night Party\nNine international feature films with director Q&As\nBattle of the Scores live music competition\nYoung Creators Co-Lab talks and workshops\nYoung Creators Showcase featuring emerging Canadian filmmakers\nFree tickets for Under-25 passholders (Official Selections)\n\nTickets & Info: tiff.net/nextwave
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/tiff-next-wave-film-festival/
LOCATION:TIFF Lightbox\, 350 King Street West\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5V 3X5
CATEGORIES:Festivals,Film & Media
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/tiff-next-wave-film-festival.png
END:VEVENT
