SUMMARY:Hamlet Dance Sword Fighting Workshop with Guillaume Côté
DESCRIPTION:Acclaimed choreographer and performer Guillaume Côté will host a free dance sword fighting workshop on Thursday\, April 16 in the dance studio of Toronto’s historic Elgin Theatre. Joined by cast member Lukas Malkowski\, the class celebrates the return of The Tragedy of Hamlet: Prince of Denmark to the stage later this month. Côté and Malkowski will teach movements directly inspired by the production’s climactic duel between their characters\, Hamlet and Laertes. Open to all\, this 90-minute experience will offer participants the unique opportunity to explore the artistry and physicality of dance sword fighting from an expert in Canada’s ballet scene. \nSpace in the workshop is limited\, email tickets@showoneproductions.ca or call 647-226-3710 to RSVP.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/hamlet-dance-sword-fighting-workshop-with-guillaume-cote/
LOCATION:The Elgin & Winter Garden Theatres\, The Elgin & Winter Garden Theatres\, 189 Yonge St.\, M5B1M4 Toronto\, Ontario\, Canada\, Toronto\, M5B 1M4
CATEGORIES:Classes & Workshops,Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/hamlet-dance-sword-fighting-workshop-with-guillaume-cote.png
END:VEVENT
